# MZ-80A SA-5510: the keyboard paths the typing case doesn't touch.
# Runs with presets/keys_overrides.ini: F6 is CLR with an explicit
# SHIFT (t), F7 is HOME with SHIFT forced off (f).
# SA-5510 letters: unshifted PC keys give capitals, so keywords are
# typed in lowercase (see mz80a_typing.keys).
#
# CLR ten times, alternating Shift+Home and the F6 override, at uneven
# spacing. Each clears a line of digits one shorter than the last; a
# CLR taken as HOME would leave digits on screen.
420 type "0123456789"
500 down ShiftKey
501 key Home
509 up ShiftKey
513 type "012345678"
588 key F6
600 type "01234567"
671 down ShiftKey
672 key Home
680 up ShiftKey
684 type "0123456"
741 key F6
753 type "012345"
806 down ShiftKey
807 key Home
815 up ShiftKey
819 type "01234"
861 key F6
873 type "0123"
911 down ShiftKey
912 key Home
920 up ShiftKey
924 type "012"
952 key F6
964 type "01"
989 down ShiftKey
990 key Home
998 up ShiftKey
1002 type "0"
1021 key F6
# Cursor left, then Shift+Left (SA-1510's left is SHIFT+right, so
# both arrive shifted), then F7 under Shift: HOME, not CLR. The line
# reads AQZ, then BASIC's error for it.
1033 type "xyz"
1057 key Left
1065 down ShiftKey
1066 key Left
1074 up ShiftKey
1074 type "q"
1086 down ShiftKey
1087 key F7
1095 up ShiftKey
1095 type "a"
1103 key Return
# GRPH (F11) ten times at uneven spacing, "a1" typed after each, in
# a REM: the line alternates graphics and A1 if every press landed.
1141 type "10 rem "
1197 key F11
1205 type "a1"
1224 key F11
1232 type "a1"
1255 key F11
1263 type "a1"
1280 key F11
1288 type "a1"
1309 key F11
1317 type "a1"
1335 key F11
1343 type "a1"
1365 key F11
1373 type "a1"
1393 key F11
1401 type "a1"
1426 key F11
1434 type "a1"
1461 key F11
1469 type "a1"
1485 key Return
1523 type "20 print chr$(65)"
1659 key Return
# BREAK (Shift+Esc) stops a running program.
1697 type "30 goto 30"
1777 key Return
1815 type "run"
1839 key Return
1877 down ShiftKey
1878 key Escape
1886 up ShiftKey
1916 type "list"
1948 key Return
